# OffsideFence concept demonstrator — gitignore
#
# This is a documentation project. There is no build artifact, no
# dependency tree, no environment to isolate. The gitignore exists so
# that the repository is not accidentally polluted by editor state
# or OS metadata when a curious reader clones it.

# --- OS metadata ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# --- Editor state ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# --- Python (in case anyone tries to run the stubs) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Node (in case anyone tries to build a docs site) ---
node_modules/
.npm
.yarn/
.pnp.*

# --- Local-only notes ---
# A file like this is fine to add, just don't commit it.
TODO.local.md
NOTES.local.md

# --- The .omx session state from the author's vault ---
# This lives in the Obsidian Vault copy of the project, not in the
# public repo, but include it here in case someone copies the
# directory wholesale.
.omx/

# --- Trailing whitespace and BOM ---
# These are not committed; some editors strip them on save.
# Listed here so a `git status` doesn't show noise.
*~
*.bak
